<decision #resource-package-publication-authority apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" blocks = [] durable_candidate = true } (
  <question ?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRG1>
  What is the canonical authoring and publication unit for a resource-native App?
  </?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRG1>
  <recommendation ?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRG2>
  Use the complete workspace ResourcePackage candidate and publish it only through a target-wide transaction followed by registry refresh/readback.
  </?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRG2>
  <options {  } [
    <option { key = "whole-package" recommended = true } (
      <title ?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRG3>
      Whole workspace ResourcePackage
      </?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRG3>
      <description ?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRG4>
      The session edits one complete package and preserves all unrelated resources.
      </?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRG4>
      <tradeoff ?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRG5>
      Publication replaces a larger tree and therefore needs exact CAS and recovery.
      </?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRG5>
    )>
    <option { key = "leaf-bundle" recommended = false } (
      <title ?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRG6>
      Leaf workflow bundle
      </?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRG6>
      <description ?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRG7>
      Continue publishing only one workflow directory.
      </?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRG7>
      <tradeoff ?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRG8>
      It cannot become authority in the separate Halfcode resource root and loses App/Agent/Material closure.
      </?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRG8>
    )>
  ]>
  <answer (
    <raw-answer ?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRG9>
    The mission and plan review require genuine whole-package publication.
    </?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRG9>
    <decision-text ?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRGA>
    Resource-native authoring SHALL use the complete workspace ResourcePackage as its candidate/publication unit; resource refs SHALL come from post-commit registry readback.
    </?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRGA>
    <rationale ?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRGB>
    Halfcode loads one explicit workspace package, while current leaf publication writes to another root and fabricates identity.
    </?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRGB>
    <evidence ?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRGC>
    WorkflowAuthoringSessionStore, runtime root bindings, EidolonAppResourceRegistryAdapter and the prerequisite plan review.
    </?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRGC>
  )>
  <confidence ?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRGD>
  1.0
  </?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRGD>
  <reversibility ?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRGE>
  low
  </?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRGE>
)>

<decision #legacy-vfs-reference-honesty apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" blocks = [] durable_candidate = true } (
  <question ?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRGF>
  How should legacy workflow bundle publication remain compatible?
  </?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRGF>
  <recommendation ?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRGG>
  Keep the explicit VFS path and return only its actual vfs ref.
  </?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRGG>
  <options {  } [
    <option { key = "vfs-only" recommended = true } (
      <title ?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRGH>
      Honest VFS compatibility
      </?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRGH>
      <description ?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRGJ>
      Legacy bundles remain under the workflow root and resolve only through the explicit VFS repository path.
      </?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRGJ>
      <tradeoff ?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRGK>
      Callers that need resource authority must migrate to package mode.
      </?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRGK>
    )>
    <option { key = "resource-alias" recommended = false } (
      <title ?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRGM>
      Construct a resource alias
      </?01M0QPAV7GHVH6TJZ66NCDMRGM>
      <description ?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARB>
      Format the workflow FQN as resource URI.
      </?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARB>
      <tradeoff ?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARC>
      The URI is absent from Halfcode registry and creates false authority.
      </?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARC>
    )>
  ]>
  <answer (
    <raw-answer ?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARD>
    Compatibility must be honest and must not claim resource authority.
    </?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARD>
    <decision-text ?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARE>
    Legacy draft/publication receipts SHALL expose vfs refs only and SHALL never construct resource refs.
    </?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARE>
    <rationale ?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARF>
    URI scheme is an authority boundary, not an interchangeable presentation.
    </?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARF>
    <evidence ?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARG>
    The legacy artifact remains physically under .eidolon/workflows and is not loaded by the resource registry.
    </?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARG>
  )>
  <confidence ?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARH>
  1.0
  </?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARH>
  <reversibility ?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARJ>
  low
  </?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARJ>
)>

<decision #fixture-kind-authority apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" blocks = [] durable_candidate = true } (
  <question ?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARK>
  How can tests cover a self-contained package without creating a second Kind authority?
  </?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARK>
  <recommendation ?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARM>
  Use a complete physical ResourcePackage as explicit fixture input and keep every KindDefinition out of production constants/catalogs.
  </?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARM>
  <options {  } [
    <option { key = "explicit-package" recommended = true } (
      <title ?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARN>
      Explicit package input
      </?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARN>
      <description ?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARP>
      The fixture carries its manifest, actual KindDefinitions and resources as the package under test.
      </?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARP>
      <tradeoff ?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARQ>
      Fixture files must be maintained as a coherent input package.
      </?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARQ>
    )>
    <option { key = "production-kind-builder" recommended = false } (
      <title ?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARR>
      Production Kind builder
      </?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARR>
      <description ?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARS>
      Eidolon code generates the KindDefinitions required by a package.
      </?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARS>
      <tradeoff ?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ART>
      This duplicates Halfcode/depa authority and turns test convenience into production semantics.
      </?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ART>
    )>
  ]>
  <answer (
    <raw-answer ?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARV>
    Published modules or explicit ResourcePackage inputs own the resource standards; Eidolon does not.
    </?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARV>
    <decision-text ?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARW>
    The canonical fixture SHALL be an explicit complete package, while production SHALL only load caller/live packages through Halfcode and depa projections.
    </?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARW>
    <rationale ?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARX>
    A fixture is test input; a production builder/catalog would be a competing authority.
    </?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARX>
    <evidence ?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARY>
    Halfcode loadResourceTree contract, depa projection APIs and current hand-built registry fixture gap.
    </?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARY>
  )>
  <confidence ?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARZ>
  0.99
  </?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9ARZ>
  <reversibility ?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9AS0>
  moderate
  </?01M0QPAV7H4Y8MR1EWDTFC9AS0>
)>
